[2026-03-14T22:40:53.974Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U4xMcgXb29wJHxu2BvUJLv","type":"tool_result","content":"  1780→- **Action**: User enters \"Quick Spike\" in Name, leaves all optional fields empty/default, clicks \"Create Project\"\n  1781→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The project \"Quick Spike\" appears in the project list with the default status, no lead, no target date, and no teams. The project card handles missing optional fields gracefully.\n  1782→\n  1783→#### Test: Create project modal validates name is required\n  1784→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1785→- **Action**: User leaves the Name field empty and clicks \"Create Project\"\n  1786→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown for the Name field (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The modal remains open. No project is created.\n  1787→\n  1788→#### Test: Cancel button closes create project modal without creating\n  1789→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. User has entered \"Draft Project\" in Name.\n  1790→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  1791→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project named \"Draft Project\" is created. The project list remains unchanged.\n  1792→\n  1793→#### Test: Create project modal can be closed by clicking backdrop\n  1794→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1795→- **Action**: User clicks the backdrop/overlay area outside the modal\n  1796→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project is created.\n  1797→\n  1798→#### Test: Create project modal can be closed with Escape key\n  1799→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1800→- **Action**: User presses the Escape key\n  1801→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project is created.\n  1802→\n  1803→#### Test: Creating a project and then opening modal again resets fields\n  1804→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has just created a project via the modal\n  1805→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Project\" button again to open the modal\n  1806→- **Expected**: All fields are reset to their defaults (Name is empty, Description is empty, Status is default, Lead is unset, Target date is unset, Teams is unset). No data from the previous creation persists in the form.\n  1807→\n  1808→#### Test: Created project appears immediately in the project list\n  1809→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects` with 2 existing projects\n  1810→- **Action**: User creates a new project \"API v3\" via the create project modal\n  1811→- **Expected**: The project list now shows 3 projects, including the newly created \"API v3\". The new project appears without requiring a page refresh.\n  1812→\n  1813→#### Test: Create project modal Lead selector can be used multiple times\n  1814→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1815→- **Action**: User selects \"Alice\" as lead, then clicks the lead selector again and changes to \"Bob\"\n  1816→- **Expected**: The lead is updated to \"Bob\". The selector works correctly on repeated use. Only one lead can be selected at a time.\n  1817→\n  1818→#### Test: Create project modal Teams selector can be toggled multiple times\n  1819→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1820→- **Action**: User selects \"Engineering\", then also selects \"Design\", then deselects \"Engineering\"\n  1821→- **Expected**: Only \"Design\" remains selected. The multi-select works correctly through multiple toggle interactions.\n  1822→\n  1823→## Project Detail Page (`/project/:projectId`)\n  1824→\n  1825→**Components**: ProjectHeader, ProjectIssuesTab, ProjectOverviewTab\n  1826→\n  1827→### ProjectHeader\n  1828→\n  1829→#### Test: Project header renders all fields for an existing project"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BLv4Wge7RFx49s6dWZ72ER","session_id":"59439265-0bb7-4237-927c-cb18dbaeb3c9","uuid":"743aec8f-5bd9-4ae0-843d-f3642c616b0b"}
